Clean, minimal, gets the job done. Map-based storage for O(1) lookups. SKU as the key since that's what identifies items. Adding the same SKU increments quantity instead of duplicating - that's how carts work in the real world.

The `UpdateQuantity` with zero or negative removes the item. Makes sense - you can't have negative stuff in your cart. `ErrItemNotFound` handles the edge cases when you're looking for something that ain't there.

I'm not working for free, but I didn't pad this with unnecessary features either. No discounts, no tax calculations, no persistence. Tests didn't ask, I didn't build.

